<section class="section" id="overview">
  <div class="section-label">Section 01</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Dataset Overview &amp; Historical Context</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Since 1934, the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences has honored the composer who most powerfully channeled a film's soul into sound. What began as a single award at the 6th ceremony has become one of Hollywood's most storied recognitions — a gold statuette carried by everyone from Max Steiner to Ludwig Göransson, spanning nine decades of orchestral romance, electronic experimentation, and cultural boundary-breaking. This dataset covers all 93 ceremonies, from <span class="highlight-text">One Night of Love (1934)</span> through <span class="highlight-text">Sinners (2026)</span>, yielding an unbroken record of who shaped what we hear on screen.
  </p>
